  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1..Highs in the low 90s inland and mid 80s across \nthe OBX expected this afternoon. Combined with dewpoints in the\nupper 60s to low 70s we are observing heat indices between \n95-100F this afternoon. While this is below heat advisory \ncriteria, it will still remain rather hot today. \n\nExpecting hot and humid conditions to continue into the end of\nthe workweek across ENC. Low level thicknesses will remain \naround 1430m and based off the offices climatological study, \nthis is forecast to result in highs in the mid to upper 90s \nacross the inland areas and upper 80s to low 90s along the OBX \nand coast Thurs/Fri before a front impacts the region Fri\nevening into Sat resulting in cooler temperatures this weekend.\nTemps may briefly warm up once again early next week as well. \n\nHeat indices are expected to peak around 105-110F Thurs and Fri\nwith a Heat Advisory in effect Thursday for most of ENC. A Heat\nAdvisory will likely be needed Friday as well unless if the\nforecast changes substantially. We encourage anyone planning on\nspending alot of time outdoors this week to take proper \nprecautions and stay hydrated.\n\nKEY MESSAGE 2...Low precip chances continue for today and\nThursday, with one or two isolated showers possible along the\nsea breeze. While we still expect several shortwaves to ride \nalong the northern periphery of an upper level ridge centered \nacross the Gulf Coast this week, a mix of cloud cover today and \nsome subsidence aloft today and into the early part of tomorrow,\nmay put a damper on precip chances with any MCS's that ride \nalong the surface ridging remaining to our west today. Because \nof this have only kept SChc PoPs along the sea breeze this \nafternoon as a result. Looks like shortwave tomorrow evening\nwill approach the mid-atlantic, bringing a slight chance of\nweakening showers and tstorms into the region. Recent model\ntrends the best energy remains to our north, and as a result we\nmay avoid all of the activity tomorrow night. However, given low\npredictability of MCS's, elected to add Schc PoPs across the CWA\nlate Thursday. \n\nA stronger northern stream shortwave is progged to push across \nthe Mid-Atlantic Friday with the attendant cold front pushing \ninto the area Fri evening into Sat bringing the best forcing \nand chances showers and storms across the area. High pressure \nbuild into the area over the weekend bringing bringing a drier \nairmass and minimal chances for storms. However, a second \nfrontal boundary looks to approach next week which could once \nagain bring increased chances for showers and storms early next \nweek.",
